within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.N_NervousSystem.N02A_Opioids.N02AE01_Buprenorphine;
model Buprenorphine_Love2015_PD_step_count
  "indirect_response_ii exposure-response sweep — Love_2015 :: Step count (Step count)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 56.3,      // [step hour À1]
    Emax = 1,  // type II effect term
    EC50 = 9e-07,  // [kg/m3; ng mL À1 × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1.3,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng mL À1 per second
equation
  response = E0/(1 - Emax*frac);   // steady state, indirect response type II
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 9, Interval = 0.018),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Buprenorphine_Love2015_PD_step_count</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Love EJ et al., <i>Veterinary anaesthesia and analgesia 42(1):17–29</i> 2015 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/vaa.12165\">doi:10.1111/vaa.12165</a>) — Step count [step hour À1] against buprenorphine ng mL À1 — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_ii.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       56.3 step hour À1 drug-free response (baseline) (R 0, Q324)
  Emax  =          1          maximal effect term (I max, Q323)
  EC50  =        0.9 ng mL À1 exposure at half of the maximal effect term (IC 50, Q322)
  gamma =        1.3          Hill coefficient (n, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0/(1 - Emax*frac)</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng mL À1 of buprenorphine per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 56.3   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (0.9 ng mL À1)  response 112.6
  exposure -> infinity  response inf</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Love_2015: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Buprenorphine_Love2015_PD_step_count;
